54:\revision{revival-bound}{The Working Draft of February 2011 gave such a type
55-parameter the implicit clause ``\EXP{\KWD{extends} \TYP{Object}}''.
56-\TYP{Any} holds every value, tuples and \TYP{()} among them, which \TYP{Object}
57-does not (the team's later Types chapter, Luchangco, 2012); \library\ are
58-written under \TYP{Any}, instantiating such parameters at tuple types, and the
59-interpreter reads the bound so.
60-The type group's paper of 2019 says the same: ``By default, each type parameter
61-has an upper bound Any'' (Park, Hong, Steele and Ryu, POPL 2019).
62-The compiled path still gives such a type parameter of a program's own
63-declarations the bound \TYP{Object} (row~412 of the revival's gap ledger), a
64-divergence that lasts until the compiled path is switched over to the
65-interpreter's library.}
